before:
This complete example supplies both tables before comparing their rows.
```sql
CREATE TABLE morning(name TEXT);
CREATE TABLE evening(name TEXT);
INSERT INTO morning VALUES('Ari'),('Bo'),('Bo');
INSERT INTO evening VALUES('Bo'),('Cy');
SELECT name
FROM morning
INTERSECT
SELECT name
FROM evening
ORDER BY name;
SELECT name
FROM morning
EXCEPT
SELECT name
FROM evening
ORDER BY name;
```
The intersection returns Bo. The second result returns Ari: it starts with morning and removes shared names.

